WEBVTT

00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:28.000
<b>Katagiri Yuichi</b>

00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:28.000
<b>High School, Second Year</b>

00:00:28.020 --> 00:00:30.450
<b>Kodan Newspaper</b>

00:00:31.170 --> 00:00:32.630
Good work.

00:00:33.130 --> 00:00:34.770
I finished the deliveries.

00:00:34.770 --> 00:00:36.600
Five hundred copies of the morning edition.

00:00:36.600 --> 00:00:38.510
You're working extra hard today.

00:00:38.510 --> 00:00:40.610
That's more than twice your usual.

00:00:40.610 --> 00:00:41.640
Thanks.

00:00:41.640 --> 00:00:44.070
Yeah, I'm short on money right now.

00:00:44.070 --> 00:00:47.150
Next month's school trip costs 
70,000 yen per person.

00:00:47.150 --> 00:00:51.030
70,000? That must be tough for you.

00:00:51.700 --> 00:00:54.440
Can you choose not to go?

00:00:54.440 --> 00:00:58.410
No way. Everyone promised to go together.

00:00:58.840 --> 00:01:01.410
Who's "everyone?"

00:01:02.740 --> 00:01:04.280
My friends.

00:01:05.580 --> 00:01:06.170
<b>Episode 1: Huh? Yuichi-kun Suspects His Friends?</b>

00:01:06.050 --> 00:01:08.630
<b>Episode 1: Huh? Yuichi-kun Suspects His Friends?</b>

00:01:09.040 --> 00:01:10.850
You did it, Yuichi!

00:01:10.850 --> 00:01:15.420
But y'know, if you'd just asked, my Dad would 
have spotted you the 70K, no problem.

00:01:15.420 --> 00:01:16.930
Shibe!

00:01:16.930 --> 00:01:20.430
Quit saying things like that! 
It's so condescending!

00:01:20.430 --> 00:01:24.460
Give him a break, Sawaragi-san. 
He didn't mean anything by it.

00:01:24.460 --> 00:01:28.230
But I think you have something else 
to say to him. Right, Kokorogi-san?

00:01:28.230 --> 00:01:29.060
Mm-hmm.

00:01:29.860 --> 00:01:31.060
I guess you're right.

00:01:31.060 --> 00:01:32.820
All right, then. Again...

00:01:33.610 --> 00:01:35.440
Good job, Yuichi!

00:01:35.900 --> 00:01:37.820
<b>Shibe Makoto</b>

00:01:35.990 --> 00:01:37.820
<b>Class president who's good at sports and comes from
 a rich family. That makes him sound perfect, but...</b>

00:01:35.990 --> 00:01:37.820
<b>He's an airhead and can be very inconsiderate, 
so he's surprisingly unpopular with girls... 
All in all, he's a hard guy to hate, though.</b>

00:01:37.820 --> 00:01:40.570
I wasn't worried about him for a minute.

00:01:40.950 --> 00:01:42.330
<b>Sawaragi Shiho</b>

00:01:40.990 --> 00:01:42.330
<b>Our class vice president, but people also
 say she's the "real" class president.</b>

00:01:40.990 --> 00:01:42.330
<b>Her father's a police officer and she had 
a strict upbringing, so she hates things 
that aren't right and is a tough fighter. 
In many ways, she's very dependable.</b>

00:01:42.330 --> 00:01:44.500
I'm looking forward to the trip.

00:01:44.700 --> 00:01:46.830
<b>Mikasa Tenji</b>

00:01:45.120 --> 00:01:46.830
<b>A genius at the top of his class. He isn't just good at 
studying, he also has top-level communication skills.</b>

00:01:45.120 --> 00:01:46.830
<b>He might look unfriendly, but I've never met anyone,
 including teachers, who would ever bad-mouth him. 
He acts as our negotiator, too.</b>

00:01:47.160 --> 00:01:49.640
W-Well done, Yuichi!

00:01:49.880 --> 00:01:51.340
<b>Kokorogi Yutori</b>

00:01:50.000 --> 00:01:51.340
<b>Nice girl who doesn't speak up much. I think 
she likes anime and stuff.</b>

00:01:50.000 --> 00:01:51.340
<b>She was bullied during first year, but now 
that she's in the same class as Sawaragi, 
there's no way the bullying could continue... 
We became friends through Sawaragi.</b>

00:01:52.650 --> 00:01:54.590
<i>Thanks, guys.</i>

00:01:56.280 --> 00:01:59.840
<i>We're all friends, now and forever.</i>

00:02:00.780 --> 00:02:02.910
<i>At least, that's what I'd always thought.</i>

00:02:03.350 --> 00:02:06.230
I have something very
 important to tell you all.

00:02:06.650 --> 00:02:11.110
The two million yen we collected 
for the school trip was stolen.

00:02:11.110 --> 00:02:12.860
Huh? No way!

00:02:12.860 --> 00:02:15.330
I'm so sorry, guys!

00:02:16.240 --> 00:02:19.990
I put the money in my locker 
yesterday during fifth period...

00:02:21.740 --> 00:02:26.150
And I locked the door, but a few
 minutes later, it was gone.

00:02:26.150 --> 00:02:30.090
Please, if the thief is here, speak up!

00:02:30.090 --> 00:02:31.840
Why the hell does she suspect us?

00:02:31.020 --> 00:02:33.130
We know who has money problems...

00:02:31.840 --> 00:02:33.760
Why did they collect cash anyway?

00:02:33.760 --> 00:02:36.110
Who's the poorest one here?

00:02:33.760 --> 00:02:36.950
There's no way the thief would admit it.

00:02:36.950 --> 00:02:39.420
<i>In the end, no one came forward.</i>

00:02:39.420 --> 00:02:45.020
<i>And the next day, for some reason, 
Sawaragi and Shibe stopped coming to school.</i>

00:02:46.500 --> 00:02:49.350
Hey, don't you think Sawaragi 
and Shibe stole it?

00:02:49.350 --> 00:02:51.600
The crying and stuff looked totally fake.

00:02:51.600 --> 00:02:54.130
This doesn't look good.

00:02:51.600 --> 00:02:54.630
Really? I'd never forgive them.

00:02:54.130 --> 00:02:56.730
Neither one is answering 
or responding to texts.

00:02:56.730 --> 00:02:58.420
<b>Stare...</b>

00:02:57.830 --> 00:03:00.240
The long weekend starts tomorrow. 
Should we check on them?

00:03:00.240 --> 00:03:02.240
<b>Tomodachi Game</b>

00:03:17.020 --> 00:03:18.340
Who is it?

00:03:23.640 --> 00:03:26.800
What's this? A letter?

00:03:28.470 --> 00:03:30.980
Sawaragi Shiho

00:03:29.130 --> 00:03:30.590
From Sawaragi?

00:03:33.280 --> 00:03:36.770
<i>"Yuichi, I have something 
important to tell you.</i>

00:03:37.450 --> 00:03:41.650
<i>I'll be waiting at the school gate 
tonight at 11:00."</i>

00:03:46.770 --> 00:03:48.740
You're late, Yuichi!

00:03:48.740 --> 00:03:50.470
G-Guys...?

00:03:51.160 --> 00:03:53.170
<b>Tomodachi Game</b>

00:03:53.660 --> 00:03:56.540
Guys, why are you all here?

00:03:57.130 --> 00:03:59.510
Huh? Why are you asking us?

00:03:59.510 --> 00:04:00.410
Huh?

00:04:00.410 --> 00:04:03.200
Don't you have something 
important to tell us?

00:04:03.200 --> 00:04:07.320
You sent this letter to our homes.

00:04:07.970 --> 00:04:11.630
I was like, "A letter? In this day and age?" 
But I know you don't have a cell phone.

00:04:11.630 --> 00:04:13.850
I thought it was gonna be a love 
confession, I was shocked.

00:04:13.850 --> 00:04:15.340
Yeah.

00:04:16.400 --> 00:04:17.400
Yuichi?

00:04:17.400 --> 00:04:20.260
<i>This isn't right.</i>

00:04:20.260 --> 00:04:23.400
<i>We're clearly being set up here.</i>

00:04:23.400 --> 00:04:24.700
Yuichi, behind you!

00:04:26.280 --> 00:04:28.280
W-What the...

00:04:28.280 --> 00:04:29.390
Let me go!

00:04:29.390 --> 00:04:30.650
What the hell are you doing?

00:04:30.650 --> 00:04:32.410
Hey... Stop!

00:04:33.660 --> 00:04:38.350
<i>Stop... it! What are you doing...</i>

00:04:38.790 --> 00:04:42.290
<i>to my friends...</i>

00:04:44.050 --> 00:04:45.430
Yuichi-kun.

00:04:46.300 --> 00:04:49.810
The most important thing 
in this world is money.

00:04:51.710 --> 00:04:53.310
Yuichi.

00:04:55.300 --> 00:04:58.560
There's something more important 
than money in this world—

00:04:58.560 --> 00:05:01.850
your friends.

00:05:04.700 --> 00:05:06.800
Yuichi! Are you okay?

00:05:06.800 --> 00:05:08.430
Sawaragi?

00:05:12.910 --> 00:05:14.950
Where is this?

00:05:14.950 --> 00:05:16.280
Is everyone oka—

00:05:17.980 --> 00:05:20.000
Hey, guys!

00:05:20.540 --> 00:05:23.790
Good morning!

00:05:27.920 --> 00:05:29.930
Who the hell is that?

00:05:29.930 --> 00:05:33.460
It's Manabu-kun. He's a character 
from an old, late-night anime.

00:05:33.460 --> 00:05:37.810
He looks cute, but steals 
children's treasures.

00:05:38.940 --> 00:05:41.400
Guess I don't need to introduce myself.

00:05:42.440 --> 00:05:43.990
So, let's get to it!

00:05:43.990 --> 00:05:47.650
Right now, you're gonna play 
a really simple game with me!

00:05:47.650 --> 00:05:48.990
Game?

00:05:48.990 --> 00:05:52.950
For each game you clear, 
you get two million yen!

00:05:52.950 --> 00:05:54.880
T-Two million yen?!

00:05:54.880 --> 00:05:57.620
Plus, there are bonus chances in each game,

00:05:57.620 --> 00:06:02.210
so you'll be able to repay your 
20 million yen debt in a jiffy!

00:06:03.100 --> 00:06:06.970
Debt? T-Twenty million?!

00:06:09.540 --> 00:06:13.440
What the hell's going on?! 
How'd we get that much debt?!

00:06:13.440 --> 00:06:14.970
Huh...

00:06:15.360 --> 00:06:18.350
You don't remember anything 
like that, Katagiri-kun?

00:06:18.350 --> 00:06:22.360
In that case, maybe the debt 
belongs to one of the others.

00:06:23.750 --> 00:06:25.320
What did you say?!

00:06:26.260 --> 00:06:27.520
Hey, Yuichi!

00:06:27.520 --> 00:06:29.340
Oh... sorry.

00:06:29.810 --> 00:06:33.100
So, Manabu-kun, what you're trying to say

00:06:33.100 --> 00:06:36.550
is that one of us five has 20 million in debt,

00:06:36.550 --> 00:06:39.540
and if we beat this game 
thing, it'll be forgiven?

00:06:39.540 --> 00:06:42.280
Yeah, yeah! Do you get it now?

00:06:42.280 --> 00:06:44.130
Oh yes, I get it...

00:06:44.550 --> 00:06:47.550
You're a crook!

00:06:47.550 --> 00:06:53.040
Even if we were in debt, you can't get away 
with abduction and confinement.

00:06:53.040 --> 00:06:56.010
This is kidnapping, plain 
and simple! It's a crime!

00:06:56.010 --> 00:06:56.820
He's right!

00:06:56.820 --> 00:06:58.850
I bet our parents are already search—

00:06:58.850 --> 00:07:00.450
Dummies!

00:07:00.450 --> 00:07:04.230
You're the ones who wanted to play!

00:07:04.980 --> 00:07:09.850
I've already received the entry fee. 10 percent 
of the 20 million yen debt, totaling...

00:07:09.850 --> 00:07:11.360
Two million yen!

00:07:11.360 --> 00:07:16.870
<i>Two million... like the school trip fund?</i>

00:07:17.410 --> 00:07:20.870
<i>Does that mean one of us is the thief?</i>

00:07:20.870 --> 00:07:23.630
If we don't play, what happens then?

00:07:23.630 --> 00:07:25.580
I'll just let you go!

00:07:25.580 --> 00:07:28.440
But I won't return 
the two million entry fee,

00:07:28.440 --> 00:07:33.020
and whoever has the 20 million 
debt will have to pay it off alone.

00:07:32.510 --> 00:07:35.470
<b>Debt: 20 million yen</b>

00:07:33.020 --> 00:07:38.520
If you do play, the debt will be split 
into five shares of four million yen each.

00:07:35.700 --> 00:07:38.520
<b>Debt: 20 million yen</b>

00:07:35.970 --> 00:07:38.520
<b>Debt: 4 million yen</b>

00:07:36.350 --> 00:07:38.520
<b>Debt: 4 million yen</b>

00:07:36.720 --> 00:07:38.520
<b>Debt: 4 million yen</b>

00:07:37.100 --> 00:07:38.520
<b>Debt: 4 million yen</b>

00:07:37.470 --> 00:07:38.520
<b>Debt: 4 million yen</b>

00:07:38.520 --> 00:07:41.210
<i>Four million yen each...</i>

00:07:41.210 --> 00:07:44.230
You can lower that by playing the game!

00:07:44.230 --> 00:07:50.390
If you lose, the debt won't increase, 
but you'll each be stuck with what's left.

00:07:52.060 --> 00:07:55.700
I'll give you five minutes, 
so think it over, okay?

00:08:06.890 --> 00:08:09.510
H-Hey, about the debt...

00:08:09.510 --> 00:08:14.260
Given the circumstances, I don't think we 
should try and figure out whose debt it is.

00:08:15.390 --> 00:08:19.350
I can't imagine they did this to trap us.

00:08:19.350 --> 00:08:23.350
They were probably in serious trouble, 
needed to find a way out,

00:08:23.990 --> 00:08:26.100
and were counting on us as friends to help.

00:08:28.890 --> 00:08:30.480
Yes, I suppose so.

00:08:30.480 --> 00:08:32.610
I could have lent them plenty!

00:08:32.610 --> 00:08:34.740
Yeah, if it's between us...

00:08:34.740 --> 00:08:37.230
...we don't need any explanation.

00:08:37.230 --> 00:08:38.990
We're friends, after all.

00:08:38.990 --> 00:08:41.220
<i>We're friends, after all.</i>

00:08:41.760 --> 00:08:45.370
<i>Really? Is that what friends are for?</i>

00:08:45.370 --> 00:08:47.930
Don't you think so, Yuichi?

00:08:47.930 --> 00:08:50.000
Yeah, w-well, I...

00:08:50.250 --> 00:08:53.760
Huh? Yuichi-kun suspects his friends?

00:08:53.760 --> 00:08:58.470
N-No way. I just wanted to 
know what the debt is for.

00:08:58.470 --> 00:09:00.560
Why would you want to know?

00:09:00.560 --> 00:09:05.110
If it was a really stupid reason, 
would you abandon your friend?

00:09:04.690 --> 00:09:09.190
<b>The spoiled rich Shibe?</b>

00:09:05.060 --> 00:09:09.190
<b>The hypocritical Shiho-sama?</b>

00:09:05.110 --> 00:09:09.190
So Yuichi-kun, which one's untrustworthy trash?

00:09:05.440 --> 00:09:09.190
<b>The sly Tenji-kun?</b>

00:09:05.810 --> 00:09:09.190
<b>The sexy Yutori-chan?</b>

00:09:09.720 --> 00:09:13.820
Or is it just that you care more 
about money than your friends?

00:09:13.820 --> 00:09:17.380
Maybe the reason doesn't matter. 
You just don't wanna waste that money.

00:09:17.380 --> 00:09:19.070
Why don't you tell everyone, then?

00:09:19.070 --> 00:09:22.580
What's most important to you, Yuichi-kun?

00:09:22.580 --> 00:09:25.970
T-The most important thing to me is...

00:09:25.970 --> 00:09:28.050
Yeah, yeah, what is it?

00:09:28.050 --> 00:09:29.330
<i>It's money.</i>

00:09:29.330 --> 00:09:30.630
<i>It's friends.</i>

00:09:31.780 --> 00:09:34.470
The most important thing to me is...

00:09:35.880 --> 00:09:37.220
Friends!

00:09:37.650 --> 00:09:39.970
Friends are more important than money!

00:09:39.970 --> 00:09:42.220
There ya go!

00:09:44.780 --> 00:09:50.520
All right then, I'll show you 
to the first game room!

00:09:50.520 --> 00:09:52.520
<b>Tomodachi Game</b>

00:09:54.190 --> 00:09:55.940
Okay, come in, come in.

00:09:55.940 --> 00:09:58.360
Eh... what is this place?

00:09:58.360 --> 00:10:01.060
When You See a Stranger, Expect a Thief.

00:09:58.650 --> 00:10:01.060
It looks like a classroom.

00:10:02.330 --> 00:10:04.800
Is the outside just a painting?

00:10:02.330 --> 00:10:05.790
Class Lesson 
When You See a Stranger, Expect a Thief.

00:10:06.300 --> 00:10:08.530
And... a Kokkuri-san?

00:10:07.210 --> 00:10:09.920
<b>Yes</b>

00:10:07.210 --> 00:10:09.920
<b>No</b>

00:10:08.530 --> 00:10:09.920
A huge ten yen coin!

00:10:09.920 --> 00:10:11.670
<b>Friendship</b>

00:10:09.940 --> 00:10:11.670
Attention, please!

00:10:11.670 --> 00:10:15.670
First of all, take your name 
tags over there.

00:10:15.670 --> 00:10:18.930
Shibe Makoto

00:10:15.670 --> 00:10:18.930
Sawaragi Shiho

00:10:15.670 --> 00:10:18.930
Mikasa Tenji

00:10:15.670 --> 00:10:18.930
Kokorogi Yutori

00:10:15.670 --> 00:10:18.930
Katagiri Yuichi

00:10:15.670 --> 00:10:18.930
Before you put them on, 
check the number on the back.

00:10:20.130 --> 00:10:21.890
Negative four million?

00:10:22.890 --> 00:10:25.890
Right. That's your current debt amount.

00:10:25.890 --> 00:10:30.810
If you clear the game and that drops 
to zero, so does your debt.

00:10:30.810 --> 00:10:33.650
But you can't show that 
number to anyone else.

00:10:33.650 --> 00:10:37.070
If you do, the amount will double.

00:10:37.070 --> 00:10:38.370
Double?

00:10:38.370 --> 00:10:40.570
Right now, that would be 
eight million in debt.

00:10:41.290 --> 00:10:44.600
We just can't show it, right?

00:10:44.600 --> 00:10:47.700
Yeah! It's okay to say it, though.

00:10:47.700 --> 00:10:50.460
That's not such a harsh rule, then.

00:10:50.460 --> 00:10:56.210
Well, seeing is believing. So let's give
 the Kokkuri-san game a shot!

00:10:56.210 --> 00:11:00.830
Put your finger on the coin and push it 
to the answer you think is right.

00:11:00.630 --> 00:11:05.310
Japan's northernmost prefecture is <b>Hokkaido.</b>

00:11:00.830 --> 00:11:05.310
Question: Japan's northernmost 
prefecture is Hokkaido.

00:11:06.810 --> 00:11:11.910
Kokkuri-san, Kokkuri-san, if you are 
present, please tell us the answer.

00:11:14.050 --> 00:11:15.610
It moved!

00:11:19.150 --> 00:11:20.530
It stopped?

00:11:21.860 --> 00:11:25.170
Ta-da! Correct answer!

00:11:25.170 --> 00:11:27.330
If that was real, you would 
have cleared the game!

00:11:27.330 --> 00:11:28.950
Just like that?

00:11:28.950 --> 00:11:29.840
Yeah!

00:11:29.840 --> 00:11:33.890
If the five good friends give the same 
answer, Kokkuri-san raises his hands.

00:11:33.890 --> 00:11:38.130
Okay, now Yutori-chan, 
try to push it toward "no."

00:11:38.130 --> 00:11:39.700
Eh? Um...

00:11:43.510 --> 00:11:48.890
Yes! If even one person's answer is different, 
Kokkuri-san will favor the minority.

00:11:49.190 --> 00:11:50.150
I see.

00:11:50.150 --> 00:11:53.480
In other words, it's a pass/fail quiz 
to see if we can all agree.

00:11:53.480 --> 00:11:57.620
There are five questions in total. 
If you clear one, you win the game.

00:11:53.480 --> 00:12:00.360
<b>- Manabu-kun selects a question reader. 
- The reader opens a numbered envelope.
- If you win, you get two million yen.
- Everyone's debt will go down 400,000 at a time.
- You may only speak when reading a question. 
(If you break the rules, your debt is doubled.)</b>

00:11:57.620 --> 00:12:00.360
Also, read the fine print over there.

00:12:00.360 --> 00:12:03.820
Finally, if you get every question wrong,

00:12:05.070 --> 00:12:06.730
last place gets a penalty!

00:12:06.730 --> 00:12:12.080
If it's game over, the person with the most 
debt has to take everyone else's, too!

00:12:10.120 --> 00:12:12.080
<b>Last place penalty</b>

00:12:13.300 --> 00:12:18.090
Lastly, since you look a little anxious, 
I'll give you some important advice:

00:12:20.590 --> 00:12:24.780
Never doubt your friends!

00:12:24.780 --> 00:12:31.730
That's the only way to have a happy
 ending to the Tomodachi Game!

00:12:32.100 --> 00:12:33.560
Onto the first game, then!

00:12:33.560 --> 00:12:35.850
Kokkuri-san game, start!

00:12:35.850 --> 00:12:38.520
The first reader is Shibe Makoto!

00:12:39.360 --> 00:12:41.280
<i>What was that look?</i>

00:12:43.280 --> 00:12:44.150
<i>Huh?</i>

00:12:44.150 --> 00:12:48.030
Question: Is the tallest mountain in Japan Mt. Fuji?

00:12:48.030 --> 00:12:50.640
<i>It's simple! We can do it!</i>

00:12:51.500 --> 00:12:52.730
Hup!

00:12:52.730 --> 00:12:57.460
Kokkuri-san, Kokkuri-san, if you are 
present, please tell us the answer.

00:12:58.710 --> 00:13:03.380
<i>We had no idea how terrifying
 the game would be.</i>

00:13:01.360 --> 00:13:03.450
<b>No</b>

00:13:02.990 --> 00:13:07.970
<b>No</b>

00:13:07.970 --> 00:13:10.810
Question one: Incorrect!

00:13:10.810 --> 00:13:14.020
The correct answer is "Yes!"

00:13:10.830 --> 00:13:12.170
<b>Yes</b>

00:13:20.020 --> 00:13:21.960
<b>- You may only speak when reading a question. 
(If you break the rules, your debt is doubled.)</b>

00:13:21.300 --> 00:13:22.530
<b>- You may only speak when reading a question. 
(If you break the rules, your debt is doubled.)</b>

00:13:32.820 --> 00:13:35.250
<i>But what does this mean?</i>

00:13:35.850 --> 00:13:38.000
<i>There's no way we'd get that wrong.</i>

00:13:38.890 --> 00:13:42.020
<i>Did someone deliberately choose "no"?</i>

00:13:42.020 --> 00:13:45.010
Question two: The reader is Sawaragi Shiho.

00:13:48.160 --> 00:13:51.350
Question: Does one plus one equal two?

00:13:52.070 --> 00:13:54.320
<i>It's too simple!</i>

00:13:54.320 --> 00:13:58.650
Kokkuri-san, Kokkuri-san, if you are 
present, please tell us the answer.

00:13:54.770 --> 00:13:58.080
<i>Someone must have just overthought 
the first question. That's it!</i>

00:13:58.650 --> 00:14:01.310
<b>Yes</b>

00:13:58.650 --> 00:14:01.370
<i>"Yes" is the only possible answer!</i>

00:14:00.960 --> 00:14:02.400
<b>No</b>

00:14:01.370 --> 00:14:04.810
"No"—Incorrect!

00:14:04.810 --> 00:14:09.900
<i>S-Someone here is a traitor. 
But for what reason?</i>

00:14:09.900 --> 00:14:12.080
<i>Actually, there </i>was<i> some trouble recently...</i>

00:14:12.950 --> 00:14:15.090
Hey, Shibe, what's up with your face?

00:14:15.770 --> 00:14:18.690
I tried to surprise Shiho with a kiss.

00:14:18.690 --> 00:14:19.610
Oh, jeez.

00:14:19.610 --> 00:14:21.330
Did you actually kiss her?

00:14:23.660 --> 00:14:25.900
She smacked me before I could.

00:14:26.510 --> 00:14:30.060
Tenji, talk to Shiho for me 
so we can make up!

00:14:30.060 --> 00:14:30.930
Absolutely not.

00:14:30.930 --> 00:14:33.760
Yuichi, I beg you! Aren't we friends?

00:14:33.760 --> 00:14:35.890
Uh, yeah...

00:14:35.890 --> 00:14:38.640
I'm not mad about Shibe anymore!

00:14:38.640 --> 00:14:40.080
O-Oh, okay.

00:14:40.080 --> 00:14:42.110
But I <i>am</i> mad about something else.

00:14:42.110 --> 00:14:43.630
About what?

00:14:47.320 --> 00:14:50.960
Well, you and Shibe are
 so casual about it...

00:14:50.960 --> 00:14:53.330
Huh? Me? What did I do?

00:14:54.140 --> 00:14:56.830
Fine. Whatever. I'll forgive him.

00:14:56.830 --> 00:14:58.000
Good.

00:14:58.000 --> 00:15:03.630
In exchange, you have to tell me a secret, 
something that the other three don't know.

00:15:03.630 --> 00:15:05.380
Why would you want to know that?

00:15:05.380 --> 00:15:08.800
Who cares? Don't overthink it, dummy.

00:15:08.800 --> 00:15:13.640
All right, fine. But don't tell
 the others. Especially Shibe.

00:15:15.000 --> 00:15:18.020
Question three. The reader is Mikasa Tenji.

00:15:18.290 --> 00:15:21.680
Question: Is the English word for Nihon "Japan"?

00:15:21.680 --> 00:15:26.150
Kokkuri-san, Kokkuri-san, if you are 
present, please tell us the answer.

00:15:24.060 --> 00:15:25.860
<b>Class Lesson 
When You See a Stranger, Expect a Thief.</b>

00:15:26.150 --> 00:15:28.030
<b>No</b>

00:15:26.150 --> 00:15:28.030
Wrong again and again!

00:15:29.520 --> 00:15:30.760
<i>Who moved it to "no"?</i>

00:15:30.760 --> 00:15:32.570
<i>Why are we 20 million yen in debt?</i>

00:15:32.570 --> 00:15:33.600
<i>Risking self-destruction...</i>

00:15:33.600 --> 00:15:35.910
<i>Is one of us holding a grudge?</i>

00:15:35.910 --> 00:15:37.790
<i>At this rate, it's over.</i>

00:15:38.230 --> 00:15:42.460
<i>At this rate, I'll begin to doubt everyone...</i>

00:15:43.760 --> 00:15:45.750
<i>and my heart will turn black.</i>

00:15:43.880 --> 00:15:46.290
<b>turn black</b>

00:15:46.290 --> 00:15:49.670
Question four. The reader 
is Katagiri Yuichi.

00:15:51.550 --> 00:15:54.260
<i>W-What the hell is this?</i>

00:15:54.260 --> 00:15:57.390
<b>Reader chooses the question.</b>

00:15:54.640 --> 00:15:56.720
<i>There's no question written.</i>

00:15:57.390 --> 00:15:59.890
<i>I have to think of one myself?</i>

00:16:01.100 --> 00:16:02.980
If the 10 yen coin goes to "yes," you clear the game.
 If the 10 yen coin goes to "no," only the reader's debt will be halved.

00:16:02.980 --> 00:16:05.830
<i>If "Yes," we advance to the next game.</i>

00:16:02.980 --> 00:16:08.860
<b>Yes</b>

00:16:02.980 --> 00:16:08.860
<b>No</b>

00:16:05.830 --> 00:16:08.860
<i>If "No," that mistake 
will keep us from winning,</i>

00:16:08.860 --> 00:16:11.600
<i>but my debt will be cut in half.</i>

00:16:12.240 --> 00:16:17.490
The person with the most debt 
has to take everyone else's, too!

00:16:15.410 --> 00:16:17.370
<b>Last place penalty</b>

00:16:17.490 --> 00:16:21.250
reader's debt will be halved.

00:16:17.870 --> 00:16:21.760
<i>I get it! The first three questions 
were the same way!</i>

00:16:21.760 --> 00:16:24.310
<i>They chose questions with
 an easy "Yes" answer</i>

00:16:24.310 --> 00:16:26.250
<i>but then picked "No" themselves.</i>

00:16:26.250 --> 00:16:28.200
Mikasa Tenji

00:16:26.250 --> 00:16:28.200
Sawaragi Shiho

00:16:26.250 --> 00:16:28.200
Shibe Makoto

00:16:26.250 --> 00:16:30.460
And they did it to cut 
their own debt in half!

00:16:32.410 --> 00:16:35.770
<i>Yeah... That must be it.</i>

00:16:37.450 --> 00:16:40.450
Look at this guy's face in Group C!

00:16:40.450 --> 00:16:43.520
He totally suspects his friends now.

00:16:43.520 --> 00:16:46.490
Will he be able to choose "yes"?

00:16:46.490 --> 00:16:48.520
It must be difficult.

00:16:48.520 --> 00:16:54.060
Humans are only able to endure difficulties 
when they see others enduring the same.

00:16:54.400 --> 00:16:58.910
They're unable to persevere in 
solitude. They can't handle it.

00:16:56.360 --> 00:16:58.910
<b>Yes</b>

00:16:56.360 --> 00:16:58.910
<b>No</b>

00:16:58.910 --> 00:17:01.160
<b>Yes</b>

00:16:59.650 --> 00:17:00.820
<i>It's "yes."</i>

00:17:01.500 --> 00:17:05.170
<i>As long as I choose "yes," 
the game will end.</i>

00:17:05.560 --> 00:17:07.760
<i>It will end, but then...</i>

00:17:08.730 --> 00:17:14.550
<i>My debt will be reduced by 400,000, 
only 1/5 of the reward for clearing it.</i>

00:17:15.160 --> 00:17:20.800
<i>But their debt is already half! 
They'd wipe out 2.4 million!</i>

00:17:20.800 --> 00:17:22.180
<i>In that case, I should, too...</i>

00:17:22.180 --> 00:17:27.630
Oh? Is he thinking there 
might be another move?

00:17:27.630 --> 00:17:29.810
If so, it would be a shame.

00:17:30.330 --> 00:17:35.320
No team has ever beat the Kokkuri-san 
game after reaching the fifth question.

00:17:35.320 --> 00:17:37.320
<i>I should pick "No", too.</i>

00:17:39.750 --> 00:17:41.450
Are you okay, Kokorogi?

00:17:41.450 --> 00:17:46.330
Y-Yeah. The same people are still 
bullying me a little. That's all.

00:17:47.380 --> 00:17:49.520
Sorry, Kokorogi.

00:17:49.520 --> 00:17:51.170
Huh? Why?

00:17:51.170 --> 00:17:57.570
The other three would probably be able to 
say something encouraging right now.

00:17:57.570 --> 00:17:58.710
No...

00:18:00.050 --> 00:18:02.450
That's good enough, Yuichi.

00:18:02.450 --> 00:18:03.140
Huh?

00:18:05.640 --> 00:18:10.570
You know, you might be the only one 
I can call a true friend, Yuichi.

00:18:10.570 --> 00:18:15.540
I really like the other three, 
but they feel a little distant.

00:18:16.500 --> 00:18:18.600
Have you noticed, Yuichi?

00:18:18.600 --> 00:18:23.280
You're the only one who
 calls me just "Kokorogi."

00:18:23.650 --> 00:18:31.250
That's because you're the only one 
that close to me. You know?

00:18:33.100 --> 00:18:36.490
Question: Is one week seven days long?

00:18:37.490 --> 00:18:40.200
<i>That's who I need to think about now...</i>

00:18:40.550 --> 00:18:41.900
Huh?!

00:18:41.900 --> 00:18:43.810
It appears that he had second thoughts.

00:18:43.810 --> 00:18:47.420
How boring! Are they going to win now?

00:18:47.420 --> 00:18:52.900
<i>The one I need to think about most now 
is the fifth reader, Kokorogi.</i>

00:18:52.900 --> 00:18:57.360
Kokkuri-san, Kokkuri-san, if you are 
present, please tell us the answer.

00:18:57.360 --> 00:19:03.950
<i>For Kokorogi, for my friends, 
I have to choose "Yes"!</i>

00:19:01.570 --> 00:19:03.990
<b>Yes</b>

00:19:04.240 --> 00:19:08.200
<b>No</b>

00:19:06.060 --> 00:19:07.170
No.

00:19:07.170 --> 00:19:09.750
<i>Why? Why?!</i>

00:19:08.540 --> 00:19:10.210
<b>Why!!?</b>

00:19:12.680 --> 00:19:19.730
<i>Someone's trying to dump all the debt 
on Kokorogi and finish after just one game!</i>

00:19:21.470 --> 00:19:23.050
<b>Last place penalty</b>

00:19:21.470 --> 00:19:27.400
<i>But if the fifth question's the same, 
the debts will balance out.</i>

00:19:29.370 --> 00:19:33.100
<i>Wait... is the fifth question different?</i>

00:19:33.100 --> 00:19:35.420
Did he figure it out?

00:19:35.420 --> 00:19:36.730
It appears so.

00:19:37.040 --> 00:19:40.610
The fifth question doesn't state 
any conditions for reducing debt.

00:19:40.610 --> 00:19:43.870
It's purely a "yes" or "no" question.

00:19:43.870 --> 00:19:49.580
But in their current state, they'll
 probably read too much into it.

00:19:49.580 --> 00:19:51.730
All right, final question!

00:19:51.730 --> 00:19:55.590
If you don't get this one right, 
it's game over.

00:19:53.920 --> 00:19:55.590
<b>Debt: 20 million</b>

00:20:00.550 --> 00:20:01.540
Question five.

00:20:01.540 --> 00:20:03.800
The reader is Kokorogi Yutori.

00:20:04.600 --> 00:20:10.360
Question: Will we always be friends?

00:20:19.570 --> 00:20:21.960
If this had been the first question,

00:20:21.960 --> 00:20:25.070
they all would have thought 
the answer was yes.

00:20:25.810 --> 00:20:32.080
But at this rate, they're all 
sure to fall straight into Hell.

00:20:32.070 --> 00:20:34.860
C'mon, c'mon everyone, 
put your fingers down!

00:20:32.080 --> 00:20:34.790
<b>Yes</b>

00:20:32.080 --> 00:20:34.790
<b>No</b>

00:20:34.860 --> 00:20:38.920
Here's a big hint: The answer 
to this question is "Yes"!

00:20:36.880 --> 00:20:38.920
<b>Yes 
No</b>

00:20:38.920 --> 00:20:41.910
Hmm, but I bet someone will pick "No"...

00:20:39.880 --> 00:20:42.970
<b>No 
Yes</b>

00:20:41.910 --> 00:20:46.050
It's all or nothing! Do you pick "No" 
and put "Yes" in the minority?

00:20:45.130 --> 00:20:46.970
<b>No
Yes</b>

00:20:46.050 --> 00:20:50.470
It'd be hilarious if everyone 
picked "No", then!

00:20:50.470 --> 00:20:52.100
All right, the moment of truth!

00:20:52.100 --> 00:20:55.850
It's over! Group C is going to 
be eliminated in round one!

00:20:57.400 --> 00:20:59.820
Wait just a second.

00:21:00.340 --> 00:21:02.820
Before we get the last vote...

00:21:04.990 --> 00:21:07.560
<b>...only speak when reading a question. 
...break the rules, your debt is doubled.)</b>

00:21:05.630 --> 00:21:07.560
You guys...

00:21:08.200 --> 00:21:12.500
Do you know what color underwear 
Sawaragi is wearing today?

00:21:14.790 --> 00:21:22.010
<b>NEXT: You Have a Lot to Say to Me, Don't You?</b>
